{{also|Diaspora|diáspora}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Diaspora}} {{qualifier|in certain senses}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|διασπορά||dispersion}}, from {{m|grc|διασπείρω||I scatter}}, from {{m|grc|διά||across}} + {{m|grc|σπείρω||I sow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/daɪˈæspəɹə/|/daɪˈæspɹə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/daɪˈæspɚɹə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-diaspora.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[dispersion]] of the [[Jews]] among the [[Gentile]]s after the [[Captivity]].
# Any similar dispersion.
#: ''The African '''diaspora''' caused a melding of cultures, both African cultures and Western ones, in many places.''
# A group so dispersed, ''especially'' Jews outside of the land of [[Israel]].
# The regions where such a dispersed group (''especially'' the Jews) resides, taken collectively.
#: ''Jews in the '''diaspora''' often have a different perspective of anti-Semitism from Israeli Jews.''
# Any dispersion of an originally [[homogeneous]] [[entity]], such as a [[language]] or [[culture]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=New Englishes: the case of Singapore|page=1|author=Joseph Foley|year=1988|passage=Small wonder that there should have been in recent years fresh talk of the '''diaspora''' of English into several mutually incomprehensible languages}}

